    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds three entries to **ADR-008's \"Record of Changes\"** section. Two are backfills of extensions that were never recorded there; one is today's ADR-038 extension.\n\n**Documentation only — no code changes.**\n\n## The gap\n\nADR-008's `## Record of Changes` section contained only:\n\n```\n- **2026-10-19:** Initial decision.\n```\n\nBut the selector engine was subsequently extended by three later ADRs:\n\n| ADR | Change | Recorded in ADR-008? |\n|---|---|---|\n| ADR-018 (2026-10-22) | `:link` / `:visited` / `:hover` + `RenderState` | ❌ |\n| ADR-026 (2026-10-26) | `:root` | ❌ |\n| ADR-038 (2026-10-28) | 14 new pseudos (structural / logical / language) | ❌ (until this PR) |\n\nA reader of ADR-008 alone would see \"Initial decision\" and assume no further changes. That's incomplete — the selector engine's pseudo-class support went from 0 → 4 (via ADR-018/026) → 18 (via ADR-038) across the session's arc.\n\n## Why backfill rather than only add ADR-038\n\nTwo options were considered:\n\n**(a) Only add ADR-038's entry.** Simpler, but perpetuates the gap for ADR-018 and ADR-026.\n\n**(b) Backfill all three with provenance notes.** Reader of ADR-008 gets the complete trajectory. Each backfilled entry is explicitly marked `(backfilled 2026-10-28)` so the historical record shows both the actual date of the change and the date the changelog entry was added.\n\n**Chose (b).** Same discipline as ADR-028's misdiagnosis correction and ADR-029's three corrections: the historical record gets corrected, not rewritten. The original \"Initial decision\" entry stays; new entries are appended with honest provenance.\n\n## What each entry records\n\n- **ADR-018 backfill**: `:link`/`:visited`/`:hover` + `RenderState`-aware matching (visited-URL set for `:visited`, hovered-element ancestor walk for `:hover`)\n- **ADR-026 backfill**: `:root` matching `<html>` (null parent or Document-type parent)\n- **ADR-038**: 14 new pseudos across structural (10) / logical (3) / language (1); notes that all extensions use the ADR-008 `SimpleKind` + `SimpleSelector` + `matches_simple` framework with zero changes to `dom::Node`, `CompoundSelector`, `Selector`, or the combinator matcher; cost per new pseudo: ~15-25 lines\n\n## What this means for future extensions\n\nADR-008's changelog is now current through ADR-038. Future selector-engine changes (ADR-039 `:has()` / `:dir()`, ADR-040 form-state pseudos, pseudo-elements) will add their own entries at the time — the pattern is now established and the historical debt is cleared.\n\n## Test count\n\n- Unchanged: 480 / 1851\n- Docs only\n- CI will confirm main still green\n\nRefs ADR-018, ADR-026, ADR-038\n",
